The term `sum(min(0, C[j] - (N - k) * A[j]))` represents the "savings" we get by choosing type 2 operations for certain columns instead of type 3. A saving occurs if `C[j] < (N - k) * A[j]`. The saving amount is `C[j] - (N - k) * A[j]` (which is a negative value, so it reduces the total cost).

To efficiently calculate `sum(min(0, C[j] - T * A[j]))` for varying `T`:
